desc: Ahh
//tags: reverb room acoustics image-source filter education surround
//author: Bernd Dormayer
//version: 1.3.3
//
// Physical room reverb:
//   Direct sound  : delay r/c, level 1/r, air absorption, stereo by facing direction (level + delay)
//   Reflections   : image-source method up to 2nd order (4 walls + floor/ceiling) plus a 24-tap early cluster,
//                   level sqrt(1-alpha)/L, walls attenuate the highs (free field: ground + two reflectors)
//   Late reverb   : 8-channel feedback delay network, length = RT60 from room volume and absorption (Eyring + air; Sabine: 0.161 * V / A),
//                   late level after Barron (falls with the distance beyond the critical distance r_c = 0.057 * sqrt(V/RT60))
// Source = the input as a point source with a stereo side path (Stereo width, Mono mix), optionally through a device model.
// Moving the source / listener produces a true Doppler effect (the delays glide).

slider1:0<0,1,1{Room,Free field}>-Mode
slider2:5.5<0.8,40,0.001>-Room width W (m)
slider3:4.5<0.8,40,0.001>-Room depth D (m)
slider4:2.6<0.8,15,0.001>-Room height H (m)
slider5:0.04<0.01,1,0.0001>-Wall alpha Top
slider6:0.04<0.01,1,0.0001>-Wall alpha Right
slider7:0.04<0.01,1,0.0001>-Wall alpha Bottom
slider8:0.04<0.01,1,0.0001>-Wall alpha Left
slider9:0.33<0.01,1,0.0001>-Floor + ceiling alpha
slider10:2.75<0,40,0.0001>-Source X (m)
slider11:0.25<0,40,0.0001>-Source Y (m)
slider12:1.5<0,15,0.0001>-Source height (m)
slider13:2.75<0,40,0.0001>-Listener X (m)
slider14:2.25<0,40,0.0001>-Listener Y (m)
slider15:1.5<0,15,0.0001>-Listener height (m)
slider16:1<0,2,1{Face source,Fixed,Along the path}>-Listener facing
slider17:0<-180,180,0.01>-Facing angle (deg, 0 = top wall)
slider18:100<0,100,0.01>-Mix dry/wet (%)
slider19:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Floor/ceiling reflections
slider20:0<-60,12,0.001>-Early reflections (dB)
slider21:0<-60,12,0.001>-Late reverb (dB)
slider22:0<-72,24,0.001>-Output (dB)
slider23:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Limiter
slider24:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Low cut
slider25:80<20,2000,0.01>-Low cut frequency (Hz)
slider26:1<0,7,1{6 dB/oct,12 dB/oct,18 dB/oct,24 dB/oct,30 dB/oct,36 dB/oct,42 dB/oct,48 dB/oct}>-Low cut slope
slider27:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-High cut
slider28:12000<1000,20000,0.1>-High cut frequency (Hz)
slider29:1<0,7,1{6 dB/oct,12 dB/oct,18 dB/oct,24 dB/oct,30 dB/oct,36 dB/oct,42 dB/oct,48 dB/oct}>-High cut slope
slider30:0<0,1,1{Pre reverb,Post reverb}>-Filter position
slider31:1<0.25,4,0.0001>-Size (room scale)
slider32:1<0.01,10,0.0001>-Decay (RT60 factor)
slider33:0<-100,100,0.01>-Tone (dark … bright)
slider34:0<0,200,0.01>-Predelay (ms)
slider35:0<0,12,1{Original,Telephone,Mobile phone,Smartphone,Walkie-talkie,Radio,Boombox,TV,Laptop,Tablet,Mini speaker,Headphones,Megaphone}>-Source model
slider36:0<0,1,1{On,Off}>-Room engine (on / off)
slider37:0<0,100,0.01>-Source distortion (%)
slider38:80<0,100,0.01>-Density (%)
slider39:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Filter bypass
slider40:0<-72,48,0.001>-Input (dB)
slider41:0<0,3,1{Off,Wall,Window,Door}>-Barrier
slider42:1.25<0,160,0.001>-Barrier position (m from back wall)
slider43:0<0,100,0.1>-Barrier open (%)
slider44:25<0,70,0.1>-Barrier damping (dB)
slider45:2.75<0,160,0.001>-Barrier element X (m)
slider46:0<0,9,1{Same as room,Concrete,Glass,Metal,Wood,Curtain,Foam,Wool,Tiles,Plaster}>-Back part material
slider47:0<-10,10,0.001>-Source EQ: high-pass shift (oct)
slider48:0<-10,10,0.001>-Source EQ: low-pass shift (oct)
slider49:0<-10,10,0.001>-Source EQ: band 1 frequency shift (oct)
slider50:0<-24,24,0.01>-Source EQ: band 1 gain offset (dB)
slider51:0<-3,3,0.001>-Source EQ: band 1 Q (oct)
slider52:0<-10,10,0.001>-Source EQ: band 2 frequency shift (oct)
slider53:0<-24,24,0.01>-Source EQ: band 2 gain offset (dB)
slider54:0<-3,3,0.001>-Source EQ: band 2 Q (oct)
slider55:0<-10,10,0.001>-Source EQ: band 3 frequency shift (oct)
slider56:0<-24,24,0.01>-Source EQ: band 3 gain offset (dB)
slider57:0<-3,3,0.001>-Source EQ: band 3 Q (oct)
slider58:0<0,8,1{Model,6 dB/oct,12 dB/oct,18 dB/oct,24 dB/oct,30 dB/oct,36 dB/oct,42 dB/oct,48 dB/oct}>-Source EQ: high-pass slope
slider59:0<0,8,1{Model,6 dB/oct,12 dB/oct,18 dB/oct,24 dB/oct,30 dB/oct,36 dB/oct,42 dB/oct,48 dB/oct}>-Source EQ: low-pass slope
slider60:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Equal loudness
slider61:0<-180,180,0.1>-Source angle (deg; Fixed: 0 = towards the front wall, Listener: 0 = at the listener)
slider63:1<0,1,1{Listener,Fixed}>-Source aim
slider62:100<25,400,0.1>-Reflectivity (% of the materials' reflection, 100 = as built)
slider64:0<0,16,0.001>-Snapshot morph (0 = off, 1-16 = snapshot, between = morph to the next)
slider65:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay
slider66:0<0,1,1{Stereo,Ping-pong}>-Delay mode
slider67:0<0,1,1{ms,Tempo}>-Delay time unit
slider68:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay link time L+R
slider69:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay link EQ L+R
slider70:50<1,4000,0.1>-Delay time L (ms)
slider71:50<1,4000,0.1>-Delay time R (ms)
slider72:8<0,12,1{1/1,1/2 dotted,1/2,1/4 dotted,1/2 triplet,1/4,1/8 dotted,1/4 triplet,1/8,1/16 dotted,1/8 triplet,1/16,1/32}>-Delay note L (tempo)
slider73:8<0,12,1{1/1,1/2 dotted,1/2,1/4 dotted,1/2 triplet,1/4,1/8 dotted,1/4 triplet,1/8,1/16 dotted,1/8 triplet,1/16,1/32}>-Delay note R (tempo)
slider74:0<0,300,0.01>-Delay tempo (BPM, 0 = project tempo)
slider75:30<0,95,0.1>-Delay feedback L (%)
slider76:30<0,95,0.1>-Delay feedback R (%)
slider77:0<-48,6,0.01>-Delay level L (dB)
slider78:0<-48,6,0.01>-Delay level R (dB)
slider79:120<20,2000,0.1>-Delay low cut L (Hz)
slider80:120<20,2000,0.1>-Delay low cut R (Hz)
slider81:10000<1000,20000,0.1>-Delay high cut L (Hz)
slider82:10000<1000,20000,0.1>-Delay high cut R (Hz)
slider83:0<0,100,0.1>-Delay tape wow + flutter (%)
slider84:0<0,100,0.1>-Delay saturation (%)
slider85:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Source model on / off
slider86:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay link level L+R
slider87:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay link feedback L+R
slider88:100<0,100,0.1>-Mix Filter (%)
slider89:100<0,100,0.1>-Mix Source model (%)
slider90:100<0,100,0.1>-Mix Delay (%)
slider91:100<0,100,0.1>-Mix Room + reverb (%)
slider92:100<0,100,0.1>-Mix Barrier (%)
slider93:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay mute L
slider94:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay mute R
slider95:0<0,40,0.01>-Barrier width (m, 0 = wall to wall)
slider96:0<0,15,0.01>-Barrier height (m, 0 = floor to ceiling)
slider97:100<50,200,1>-Barrier door / window size (%)
slider98:100<0,200,0.1>-Source width (%)
slider99:0<0,24,0.01>-Delay ducking (dB)
slider100:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Motion
slider101:0<0,2,1{Source,Listener,Both}>-Motion moves
slider102:0<0,7,1{Circle,Left - right,Front - back,Up - down,Pass-by,Square,Wave,Drawn}>-Motion pattern
slider103:0.25<0.02,10,0.001>-Motion rate (Hz)
slider104:2<0.1,20,0.01>-Motion size (m)
slider105:0<0,360,1>-Motion start (deg)
slider106:0<0,1,1{Clockwise,Counter-clockwise}>-Motion direction
slider107:0<0,2,1{Listener,Own spot,Room center}>-Motion around
slider108:0<0,8,1{Hz,8 bars,4 bars,2 bars,1 bar,1/2,1/4,1/8,1/16}>-Motion tempo
slider109:0.5<0,5,0.01>-Motion glide (s)
slider110:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Input mono mix
slider111:0<0,100,0.1>-Source call: duplex (%)
slider112:0<0,100,0.1>-Source call: codec artifacts (%)
slider113:0<0,100,0.1>-Source call: dropouts (%)
slider114:0<0,3,1{Off,Narrowband,Wideband,Super-wideband}>-Source call: line bandwidth
slider115:0<0,3,1{Clean,Tape,Analog,Lo-Fi}>-Delay type
slider116:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Delay repeats through the device
slider117:0<0,100,0.1>-Distance perspective (%)
slider118:1<0,16,0.1>-Motion Doppler (0 = off, 1 = natural, 2 … 16 = boosted)
slider119:0<0,3,1{Off,Hard (asphalt),Grass,Snow}>-Free field: ground reflection
slider120:0<0,5,1{Off,Facade,Glass,Rock,Fence,Hedge}>-Reflector 1 material
slider121:0<0,200,0.01>-Reflector 1 X (m)
slider122:0<0,200,0.01>-Reflector 1 Y (m)
slider123:0<0,180,0.1>-Reflector 1 angle (deg)
slider124:0<0,640,0.01>-Reflector 1 length (m)
slider125:0<0,40,0.01>-Reflector 1 height (m)
slider126:0<0,5,1{Off,Facade,Glass,Rock,Fence,Hedge}>-Reflector 2 material
slider127:0<0,200,0.01>-Reflector 2 X (m)
slider128:0<0,200,0.01>-Reflector 2 Y (m)
slider129:0<0,180,0.1>-Reflector 2 angle (deg)
slider130:0<0,640,0.01>-Reflector 2 length (m)
slider131:0<0,40,0.01>-Reflector 2 height (m)
slider132:12<-12,24,1>-Reflector 1 level (dB)
slider133:12<-12,24,1>-Reflector 2 level (dB)
slider134:0<0,1,1{On,Off}>-Reflectors bypass
slider135:0<0,1,1{On,Off}>-Doppler when dragging by hand
slider136:0<0,1,1{Stereo,5.1}>-Output format
slider137:0<0,1,1{ITU,ITU}>-Loudspeaker layout (always ITU)
slider138:30<15,45,0.1>-ITU front angle (deg)
slider139:110<90,150,0.1>-ITU surround angle (deg)
slider140:1.2<0.3,3,0.01>-Loudspeaker height (m)
slider141:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-LFE
slider142:0<0,1,1{80 Hz,120 Hz}>-LFE crossover
slider143:0<-24,10,0.1>-LFE level (dB)
slider144:100<0,100,0.1>-Phantom ... discrete center (%)
slider145:0<0,1,1{Follows the listener,Fixed in the room}>-Loudspeaker ring
slider146:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Source snaps to a speaker
slider147:0<-24,6,0.1>-5.1 level L (dB)
slider148:0<-24,6,0.1>-5.1 level R (dB)
slider149:0<-24,6,0.1>-5.1 level C (dB)
slider150:0<-24,6,0.1>-5.1 level Ls (dB)
slider151:0<-24,6,0.1>-5.1 level Rs (dB)
slider152:0<0,2,1{Front,Rear,Around}>-5.1: delay echoes (left / right) on
slider153:1<0,3,1{12 dB,24 dB,48 dB,96 dB}>-LFE filter slope (per octave)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
in_pin:input 3
in_pin:input 4
in_pin:input 5
in_pin:input 6
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output
out_pin:center output
out_pin:LFE output
out_pin:left surround output
out_pin:right surround output

// all keys go to the plugin while its window has the focus (spaces in snapshot names) - REAPER: FX window menu,
// "Send all keyboard input to plug-in" turns it off per instance (then Space = play / stop again)
options:want_all_kb

@init
// THE VERSION, once: the footer text (the desc line and //version above must say the same)
strcpy(#verstr, "V 1.3.3 - developed with AI assistance");
ext_noinit = 1;                            // do not re-run @init at every playback start
gfx_ext_retina = 1;
C_SND = 343;
NT = 49; NIMG = 25; NCL = 24; TS = 64; NSL = 119; NSN = 119;               // taps: 0 direct, 1-6 first order (N E S W floor ceiling), 7-24 second order, 25-48 early cluster; NSL = slider count, NSN = sliders in a snapshot

MAXIN   = ceil(srate * 2.2) + 8;         // input delay line: 2nd-order images of the largest room (~480 m) + ITD + pre-delay
LINEMAX = ceil(srate * 0.3) + 8;         // per FDN line
APMAX   = ceil(srate * 0.06) + 8;        // per diffusion allpass

// SAVED STATE at FIXED addresses (snapshots, names, view): the buffers below depend on the sample rate, so anything
// placed after them would move when REAPER re-runs @init with another rate (e.g. after loading a project) - and the
// state restored by @serialize would be lost. @serialize uses the same constants (it can run before or after @init).
uslot = 64;                             // snapshots: 16 x 64 (64 … 1087)
vopt  = 2048;                           // view options + GUI arrays + snapshot names (2048 … ~8100)
ibuf    = 16384;                        // the rings start here (8192 … 16383 above it: ser_scr, scratch for loading the state in @serialize)
// THE DELAY LINES (rings) depend on the sample rate: input line, 8 + 4 FDN lines, 4 allpasses, the two delay lines and the
// side line of the delay - one after the other from ibuf. Everything else (tables, per-tap arrays, coefficients) sits at a
// fixed address (arr), so the rings can be laid out again when the sample rate changes without @init (see srsetup).
function srlayout() (
  MAXIN   = ceil(srate * 2.2) + 8;
  LINEMAX = ceil(srate * 0.3) + 8;
  APMAX   = ceil(srate * 0.06) + 8;
  fdnbase = ibuf + MAXIN;
  apbase  = fdnbase + 8 * LINEMAX;
  fdn2base = apbase + 4 * APMAX;           // 2nd network (neighbor room behind the barrier): 4 lines
  DLMAX = ceil(srate * (srate > 192000 ? 1.02 : 4.05)) + 8;   // delay lines: 4 s (above 192 kHz 1 s)
  DLMAX = min(DLMAX, floor((4194304 - 64 - (fdn2base + 4 * LINEMAX) - 2 * MAXIN) / 2));   // never into the fixed area above
  dlL = fdn2base + 4 * LINEMAX; dlR = dlL + DLMAX; sbuf = dlR + DLMAX; esbuf = sbuf + MAXIN;   // esbuf: the echoes' own left / right difference (5.1: it can sit on the rear pair)
  // RoomservicePro: the REAR network (8 lines, 5.1 only) sits after the rings of the 1.0 - their layout is untouched. Its lines
  // get the full length where the memory allows it (below 192 kHz always); above, they are shortened (never the 1.0 rings)
  fdnBbase = esbuf + MAXIN; LINEMAXB = max(64, min(LINEMAX, floor((4194304 - 64 - fdnBbase) / 8)));
);
srlayout();
arr     = 4194304 + 12000;              // fixed: per-tap arrays, tables, coefficients, filter states (… about + 20000)

// per-tap arrays (stride TS): x = target, c = current, o = old set during a crossfade
xDL = arr; xDR = xDL + TS; xGL = xDR + TS; xGR = xGL + TS; xA = xGR + TS; cDL = xA + TS; 
cDR = cDL + TS; cGL = cDR + TS; cGR = cGL + TS; cA = cGR + TS; lpL = cA + TS; lpR = lpL + TS; 
tapT = lpR + TS; tapG = tapT + TS; tapOn = tapG + TS; tapZ = tapOn + TS; 


oDL = tapZ + TS; oDR = oDL + TS; oGL = oDR + TS; oGR = oGL + TS; oA = oGR + TS; 
olpL = oA + TS; 
olpR = olpL + TS; tIX = olpR + TS; tIY = tIX + TS; tIZ = tIY + TS; 

fzSs = 4194304 + 50400; memset(fzSs, 0, 40);   // Source: filter states of the stereo side (layout as fzS: HP 0-7, LP 8-15, bands 16-21, first order 32-35)
// MIX without cancellation (Filter, Source model): complementary coefficients and the states of the phase-matched dry path
FAP = 4194304 + 50500; memset(FAP, 0, 80);                     // Filter: dry path states, L (0-39) and R (40-79)
lcCc = 4194304 + 50600; lcFc = lcCc + 20; hcCc = lcFc + 4; hcFc = hcCc + 20;   // Filter: complements (low cut -> its low-pass, high cut -> its high-pass)
fzCc = 4194304 + 50700;                                          // Source: complements of the model's high-pass (0-19, 40-42) and low-pass (20-39, 44-46)
FZA = 4194304 + 50800; memset(FZA, 0, 120);                     // Source: dry path states, mid (0-59) and side (60-119)
FZO = 4194304 + 50950; memset(FZO, 0, 44);                      // Source: dry path through the 4x anti-alias filters + DC blocker, mid (0-21), side (22-43)
// ALLOCATOR for the fixed (sample-rate independent) areas added since alloc(n) hands out the next n slots from
// 4194304 + 121000 upwards (above everything placed by hand: the map below). No hand-picked offsets any more - two areas
// cannot overlap. Hand-placed map (offsets from 4194304): 0 dsc (snapshot descriptions), 4096 snapv/gchg/gtouch/gval/gheld,
// 6000 anaR (tempo analysis), 9000 dptab (delay presets), 12000 arr (per-tap arrays, tables, coefficients - the delay lines sit at ibuf), 30000 abSt (A / B),
// 31000 mtx (menu transforms), 32000 urb (My rooms; + 1900 rmX / rmY), 40000 MTDP (drawn path), 41000 MTDS (stored paths), 44200 LBB (labels),
// 45000 MTAP (Own spot), 45100 MZR (module boxes), 50000 fcLog/fdA/fdSM (3 x TS), 50400 fzSs, 50500 FAP, 50600 lcCc.., 50700 fzCc, 50800 FZA,
// 50950 FZO, 51000 PT (62 x 20), 53000 UNB/RDB/UBS (undo + redo: 2 x 20 x USTR + USTR), 62000 uslotR (snapshot reflectors), 120000 fqGc (8);
// the spectrum buffers (SPB …) come from allocA / alloc above 121000
ALC = 4194304 + 121000;
MZR = 4194304 + 45100;   // [id * 4 … + 3] = screen box of each module card (last full frame), [80 + id] = its frame stamp mzfr
MTAP = 4194304 + 45000;   // the user-defined spot of Around > Own spot: [0] x, [1] y (slider units), [2] = 1 when set (saved via @serialize)
MTDS = 4194304 + 41000;   // four stored drawn paths (4 x 770, as MTDP) + [3080] the slot in use (saved via @serialize)
MTDP = 4194304 + 40000;   // drawn motion path: 256 points (x, y) at equal TIME steps, -1 … 1 of Size around the center; [512] = 256 when one was drawn, [513] = its duration in s, [514 …769] the heights (the same scale) (saved via @serialize)
// Bump allocator: returns the current offset ALC and advances it by n slots.
function alloc(n) local(p) ( p = ALC; ALC += n; p; );
function bpdrd(buf, d) local(rp, i, f, ym, y0, y1, y2, c1, c2, c3) ( rp = bpdW - d; i = floor(rp); f = rp - i; ym = buf[(i - 1) & 65535]; y0 = buf[i & 65535]; y1 = buf[(i + 1) & 65535]; y2 = buf[(i + 2) & 65535]; c1 = 0.5 * (y1 - ym); c2 = ym - 2.5 * y0 + 2 * y1 - 0.5 * y2; c3 = 0.5 * (y2 - ym) + 1.5 * (y0 - y1); ((c3 * f + c2) * f + c1) * f + y0; );   // 4-point Hermite read, d >= 2 samples
cvY = 0; function allocA(n) local(p) ( p = ALC; (p % 65536) + n > 65536 ? p = (floor(p / 65536) + 1) * 65536; ALC = p + n; p; );   // for fft(): the buffer must not cross a 65536 boundary
// ---- RoomservicePro: the loudspeaker list ----
// Channel order = REAPER 5.1: 0 L, 1 R, 2 C, 3 LFE, 4 Ls, 5 Rs (room for 8 channels: 7.1 adds entries, nothing else changes).
// Per channel (8 values): x, y, z in meters in room coordinates, the azimuth in degrees on the ring (0 = ahead, + = right), 1 for a
// surround ARRAY (Film), 0 otherwise. THE RING SITS ON THE LISTENER: the listener is the mixing position, the loudspeakers are his
// monitoring around him - a reflection from the wall he stands near arrives from that side, early and loud, as it does in the
// room. The ring turns with the listener's facing (Fixed = towards the screen wall, the default). Ring in the room (slider145):
// the listener is held in the middle of the room, facing the screen wall - the source pans across the loudspeakers like in a
// cinema panner and the room adds its acoustics (seen from the middle). base[60], base[61] = the ring's center, base[62] = its
// radius, base[63] = its turn (radians, 0 = towards the top wall).
MMCAP = 24; mmB = alloc(5 * MMCAP); mmN = 0;   // the small In / Out meters in the module headers: x, y, scale, offsets (GUI)
SPKN = 6; SPKL = alloc(64); SPKG = alloc(64); qSnapK = -1;   // SPKL: read by the audio thread (@block), SPKG: the same list for the GUI - every thread fills its own, so no variable is written by both
function spkset(base, ch, x, y, z, az, arr) local(p) ( p = base + ch * 8; p[0] = x; p[1] = y; p[2] = z; p[3] = az; p[4] = arr; p[5] = 0; );
// the ring: ITU angles from the sliders (L / R +-front, Ls / Rs +-surround), Film with the fixed angles of a cinema seen from the
// mixing position (L / R +-25, C 0, the surround arrays centered at +-100 degrees); radius 30 % of the smaller room side
function spkgeo(base, rx, ry, rot) local(W, D, z, R, k, az, a) (
  W = slider2 * slider31; D = slider3 * slider31; z = min(slider140, slider4 * slider31 - 0.1);
  base[60] = rx; base[61] = ry; base[63] = rot;
  R = max(0.3, min(W, D) * 0.3);
  k = 0; loop(5,
    az = slider137 < 0.5 ? (k == 0 ? -slider138 : (k == 1 ? slider138 : (k == 2 ? 0 : (k == 3 ? -slider139 : slider139))))
                         : (k == 0 ? -25 : (k == 1 ? 25 : (k == 2 ? 0 : (k == 3 ? -100 : 100))));
    a = az * $pi / 180 + rot;
    spkset(base, k == 3 ? 4 : (k == 4 ? 5 : k), rx + sin(a) * R, ry - cos(a) * R, z, az, slider137 >= 0.5 && k >= 3);
    k += 1; );
  base[62] = R;
  spkset(base, 3, rx, ry, z, 0, 0);   // LFE: no direction (it is not panned), the entry only keeps the list complete
);
spkgeo(SPKL, slider13 * slider31, slider14 * slider31, 0); spkgeo(SPKG, slider13 * slider31, slider14 * slider31, 0);
fcLog = 4194304 + 50000; fdA = fcLog + TS; fdSM = fdA + TS; dDL = alloc(TS); dDR = alloc(TS); mtRmp = 0; itdN = NIMG;   // tap ramps while a motion runs
HSN = 32; xHL = alloc(10 * HSN); xHR = xHL + HSN; cHL = xHR + HSN; cHR = cHL + HSN; hdsL = cHR + HSN; hdsR = hdsL + HSN; oHL = hdsR + HSN; oHR = oHL + HSN; ohdsL = oHR + HSN; ohdsR = ohdsL + HSN; memset(xHL, 0, 10 * HSN);   // head shadow (direct + first AND second order, taps 0-24): far-ear low-pass per tap
nfSL = nfSR = 0; xNF = cNF = 0; nfA = exp(-2 * $pi * 250 / srate);   // near field: low shelf on the direct sound below 1 m
// LINE MODULATION as a random walk: every 150 ... 400 ms a line draws a new target and glides to it
// through two one-poles (150 ms) - never periodic, so a held note behind a wall does not "breathe" in a rhythm, and the lines
// drift independently (more decorrelation). Deterministic (Park-Miller, re-seeded at every playback start): the same render twice sounds identical
BPDM = alloc(65536); BPDS = alloc(65536); bpdW = 0; bpdC = 0; bpdO = 0; bpdI = 0; bpdF = 1; bpdFI = 0; bpdOnP = 0; bpdKP = 1;   // Room off + Motion - the Doppler delay of the stereo panner path (mid, side)
PLQ = alloc(64); mtRB = alloc(3072); mtRSm = alloc(512); mtRBz = alloc(1024); mtRSz = alloc(256); SDFBUF = alloc(80); WFB = alloc(8 * 64);   // WFB: the wavefronts of the waves view (particles) // SDFBUF: the strokes of a smooth icon // the stroke being drawn (up to 1024 points, meters) and its resampled copy // (mtRBz / mtRSz - the height of every point)
MDS = alloc(100); mdSd = MDS; mdTg = MDS + 20; mdV1 = MDS + 40; mdV2 = MDS + 60; mdCn = MDS + 80;   // 20 lines (8 + 4 + 8 rear, RoomservicePro)
// Re-seeds the 12 line-modulation random walks (8 main FDN lines + 4 neighbor-room lines): seeds, targets, values, first countdowns
function modreset() local(k) ( k = 0; loop(20, mdSd[k] = 1234 + k * 7919; mdTg[k] = mdV1[k] = mdV2[k] = 1; mdCn[k] = (k + 1) * 0.02 * srate; k += 1; ); );
modreset(); mdK = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.15 * srate));
// one step of line k's walk: the read offset 0 ... 2 (x moddep)
function modstep(k) (
  mdCn[k] -= 1;
  mdCn[k] <= 0 ? ( mdSd[k] = (mdSd[k] * 16807) % 2147483647; mdTg[k] = 2 * mdSd[k] / 2147483647; mdSd[k] = (mdSd[k] * 16807) % 2147483647; mdCn[k] = (0.15 + 0.25 * mdSd[k] / 2147483647) * srate; );
  mdV1[k] += (mdTg[k] - mdV1[k]) * mdK; mdV2[k] += (mdV1[k] - mdV2[k]) * mdK;
);
// CALL LINE (source, devices only): STFT stage for codec artifacts and packet loss - frame 512 at 44.1 / 48 kHz
// (11 ms, as the 10-20 ms frames of speech codecs), 1024 at 88.2 / 96, 2048 above; hop 1/4, sqrt-Hann in and out
// (sum of the products = 2 -> scale 1 / (2 N), EEL's ifft is not normalized). The fft buffer must not cross a 65536 boundary.
QLN = srate > 130000 ? 2048 : (srate > 66000 ? 1024 : 512); QLH = QLN / 4; qlSc = 1 / (2 * QLN);
qlF = alloc(8192); floor(qlF / 65536) != floor((qlF + 4095) / 65536) ? qlF = ceil(qlF / 65536) * 65536;
// call-line buffers: STFT in / out frames, window, per-bin magnitude / phase and band maps (codec, envelope), duplex and distortion states
qlIn = alloc(2048); qlOut = alloc(2048); qlW = alloc(2048); qlMg = alloc(1032); qlPh = alloc(1032); qlBd = alloc(1032); dvS = alloc(80); memset(dvS, 0, 80); dvPk = 1; dtL1 = dtL2 = dtR1 = dtR2 = 0; dtyC = 0; qlBM = alloc(32); qlDM = alloc(2048); qlDS = alloc(2048); qlC = alloc(32); qlS = alloc(16); qlEb = alloc(1032); qlEP = alloc(72); odS = alloc(160); memset(odS, 0, 160); odOn = sdrL = sdrR = 0; memset(qlS, 0, 16);
// Sets up the call-line codec per sample rate: FFT size QLN, sqrt-Hann window, codec and envelope band maps, frames per 20 ms packet.
function qlsetup() local(k, f)
(
  QLN = srate > 130000 ? 2048 : (srate > 66000 ? 1024 : 512); QLH = QLN / 4; qlSc = 1 / (2 * QLN);
  k = 0; loop(QLN, qlW[k] = sqrt(0.5 - 0.5 * cos(2 * $pi * k / QLN)); k += 1; );
  // codec bands above 1 kHz in quarter octaves (-1 = below: always coded)
  k = 0; loop(QLN / 2 + 1, f = k * srate / QLN; qlBd[k] = f < 1000 ? -1 : min(23, floor(log(f / 1000) / log(2) * 4)); k += 1; );
  // third-octave bands from 100 Hz: the spectral envelope the codec's bit allocation follows
  k = 0; loop(QLN / 2 + 1, f = k * srate / QLN; qlEb[k] = f < 100 ? 0 : min(34, 1 + floor(log(f / 100) / log(2) * 3)); k += 1; );
  qlPF = max(1, floor(0.02 * srate / QLH + 0.5));                 // frames per 20 ms packet
);
// Clears the codec's buffers and state (in/out, magnitude, phase, delay lines, band mask, counters, noise seed) at playback start.
function qlclear() ( memset(qlIn, 0, 2048); memset(qlOut, 0, 2048); memset(qlMg, 0, 1032); memset(qlPh, 0, 1032); memset(qlDM, 0, 2048); memset(qlDS, 0, 2048);
  k0 = 0; loop(32, qlBM[k0] = 1; k0 += 1; ); qlPos = qlCnt = qlDP = 0; qlPC = 0; qlBad = 0; qlLN = 0; qlPG = 1; qlRs = 4711; );
// Resets the duplex (speakerphone) simulation: filters, hold/dip/cooldown state, gains to 1, and its noise seed.
function dqclear() ( dqF = dqS = dqPk = 0; dqAct = 0; dqHold = 0; dqAg = dqGg = 1; dqDip = dqCool = 0; dqRs = 977; );
qlsetup(); qlclear(); dqclear(); qlOnL = 0; lastqlBW = -1;
GONN = 512; gonB = alloc(2 * GONN); memset(gonB, 0, 2 * GONN); gonP = gonC = 0; gonPk = 0.001;   // goniometer: every 4th output sample, L / R
EDN = 1024; edB0 = alloc(4 * EDN); edB1 = edB0 + EDN; edB2 = edB1 + EDN; edB3 = edB2 + EDN; memset(edB0, 0, 4 * EDN); edi = 0;   // early scattering allpasses
// ---- RoomservicePro: the 5.1 renderer - direct sound and early reflections per loudspeaker (see vbap5 in settap, and @sample) ----
// per tap: five loudspeaker gains (L R C Ls Rs; the LFE is not panned) - target qG5x, current qG5c, old set qG5o (scene crossfade);
// qLP / qLPo: the tap's wall / air filter state for the loudspeaker read (the ear reads of the stereo path keep their own)
qG5x = alloc(5 * TS); qG5c = alloc(5 * TS); qG5o = alloc(5 * TS); qLP = alloc(TS); qLPo = alloc(TS); memset(qG5x, 0, 17 * TS);
// per sample, five values each: direct, early, their settled parts, the old set's parts, near-field state, tail, output, room sound, steering, bypass, meters
QP5 = alloc(128); qDR = QP5; qER = QP5 + 8; qSDR = QP5 + 16; qSER = QP5 + 24; qODR = QP5 + 32; qOER = QP5 + 40; qNF = QP5 + 48; qLT = QP5 + 56; qO = QP5 + 64; qRM = QP5 + 72; qST = QP5 + 80; qBY = QP5 + 88; qPK = QP5 + 96; qVD = QP5 + 104; qVR = QP5 + 112; memset(QP5, 0, 128);   // qVD / qVR: peaks of the direct sound / the reflections per loudspeaker (the 5.1 vectorscope)
qED = alloc(10 * EDN); memset(qED, 0, 10 * EDN); qEDL = alloc(10);   // early scattering: two allpasses per loudspeaker (lengths, see q5edset)
qSTS = alloc(40); memset(qSTS, 0, 40);                                // bass steering: per loudspeaker the low and the high split (2 + 2 biquads)
qBSS = alloc(16); qDKS = alloc(8); qPKS = alloc(16); memset(qBSS, 0, 40);   // tone shelf, dark low-pass, coincidence peak - per loudspeaker
qFS = alloc(100); qFAS = alloc(200); memset(qFS, 0, 300);            // Filter module (post) per loudspeaker: the chain (20 states), the phase-matched dry path (40)
qLMD = alloc(4 * 590); memset(qLMD, 0, 4 * 590);                     // limiter look-ahead lines of C, Ls, Rs, LFE (L / R use the stereo ones; LMLA <= 590)
// ---- RoomservicePro: the LFE - the direct sound alone (no reflections, no reverb: a subwoofer carries the source, not the
// room), low-passed at 80 or 120 Hz (4th-order Linkwitz-Riley), with its own level. The mono of the direct sound is the panned
